--- per-subject coupling (P-1b / P-1c analogue): RETIRED, underpowered by design ---
  P-8 measured this on per-channel LDA informativeness (non-saturating). At the observed effect sizes it needs about 151 subjects at rho = -0.226 and 351 at rho = +0.149. The binding constraint is cohort size, not measurement, so the threshold-change vs F1-change correlation is reported as underpowered by design and NOT run.

